body":"<!--\r\nPlease target the `master` branch. We will take care of backporting relevant fixes to older versions.\r\n\r\nBefore submitting, please read our checklist for new contributors:\r\nhttps://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/engine/introduction.html#checklist-for-new-contributors\r\n-->\r\n\r\nFixes https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/118101\r\n\r\nThe PR basically sets the animation section's end to be the animation length when AnimationNodeAnimation's `use_custom_timeline` and `stretch_time_scale` are both enabled. (This effectively just plays the original animation at a different speed)\r\n\r\nIn https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/91765, I incorrectly set the animation section's end to be the custom timeline's length. However, AnimationNodeAnimation had been relying on the buggy behavior in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116002, which allowed it to evaluate keys after the incorrect animation section, which is why this error managed to stay hidden.\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116046 fixed the buggy behavior, revealing the error in AnimationNodeAnimation.","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":1332303119,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMzMyMzAzMTE5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/regression","name":"regression","description":"","color":"ff63ac","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666705648,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA1NjQ4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:animation","name":"topic:animation","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":14236899,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4A2Tzj","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/24","html_url":"https://g